Origin: EmberBSD station disconnect recovery and regression, 2026-10-11.
Preserve Broadcom/OpenBSD authorship and licence in the modified source.
A physical CM5 loses its 2.4 GHz association while the host remains in RUN.
Subscribe to peer disconnect indications, process DEAUTH/DISASSOC, and use
LINK flags rather than status/reason to determine link direction. Ignore
stale peers, stopped/scanning stations and AP mode. Safe report metadata
supports physical verification without printing addresses or key material.
Also reconcile RUN against two valid firmware association samples when
CYW43455 silently loses the link. Queue queries outside the watchdog and
invalidate old generations before state transitions.
Reference semantics: Linux a5ebb76233b79db01e82e061173cb73c6d2b5c6b
brcmfmac/cfg80211.c and OpenBSD c27e9422e69bb315a6b6c6fbc4913e2a96c50796
sys/dev/ic/bwfm.c. See ember/boot/bwfm-link-events.md for validation limits.

